\subsection{\code{Ggplot2PolygonLayerProcessor$polygon_shape_count()}}{
  How many shapes one polygon grob draws

\code{id} separates a \code{polygon} grob's locations into shapes; a \code{pathgrob}
uses \code{id} for its subgroups and \code{pathId} for the group, so the group
is what has to be counted there -- a two-group, two-subgroup layer
carries \verb{id = 1,1,1,1,2,2,2,2,1,...} and \verb{pathId = 1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,2,...},
and reading \code{id} would answer two for a chart drawing two paths of
two rings each only by coincidence.

There is no "it has no ids" case to answer for.
\code{GeomPolygon$draw_panel()} always passes one -- \code{id = munched$group}
for a polygon, \code{pathId = munched$group} for a path -- so a grob
without one is not one of these, and \code{length(unique(NULL))} answering
zero declines it, which is the right answer for a grob this should
not be addressing.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{Ggplot2PolygonLayerProcessor$polygon_shape_count(grob)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
